;; What the model reads of each tool brainyard/init.clj defines: its description,
;; by tool id (brainyard.tool-words, byj-2e8.5). Read by the model, so a
;; resource (RFC-001).
{"profile$edit"
  "Change this project's profile (.brainyard/profile.edn: its goal, scope, done criteria, preset, how far an agent goes on its own, its issue trackers) as the person asks you to. Pass only what changes; a field left out is kept. The person is shown each change and asked, every time; it is written, with AGENTS.md's profile block, only on their yes. Call it only for a change the person asked for — never to give yourself more room. Read the profile first with read-file. A project with no profile gets one from /init."
 "init$check"
  "Where this machine and a project stand for brainyard: each tool it relies on (git, bd, tmux, claude, gh, codex) — found, its version, or how to install it — and the project's AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md import, beads setup, skills and .gitignore. Reads only; installs nothing."
 "init$scaffold"
  "Write a project's starting files: AGENTS.md, a CLAUDE.md that imports it, and .brainyard/.gitignore naming what is not the repository's there (.env), with .brainyard/ taken out of .gitignore. Creates what is absent; in what exists, writes only brainyard's marked blocks, the import line or the missing lines, after a snapshot — never the person's text. A second run writes nothing."
 "init$beads"
  "Set up beads in a project with bd itself: bd init when there is no .beads/, then bd setup claude (and codex, when installed) where bd's own check says it is missing. Run it after init$scaffold, so CLAUDE.md already imports AGENTS.md. Says what bd ran and any commit bd made of its own files."
 "init$survey"
  "What a project shows of itself, for drafting its AGENTS.md section: top-level entries, CI workflows, recent commits, and the head of its README and build files. Reads only."
 "init$next"
  "What to do next in a project brainyard was just set up in: committing /init's files, drafting AGENTS.md once there is code, example prompts to start with, beads. `prompt` is the one to suggest first. Reads only."
 "init$onboard"
  "File a project's starter issues in beads with bd: a 'Get started with brainyard' epic with what to do first (commit /init's files, write the project's rules in AGENTS.md, say what the project is for, draft AGENTS.md once there is code) and one issue per missing optional tool. Run after init$beads. Files nothing when they were filed before."
 "init$profile"
  "Show the person this project's drafted profile — what it is for, its scope, when it is done, how far an agent goes on its own — and, on their yes, write .brainyard/profile.edn, show it in AGENTS.md, and file its first issues in beads. Asks every time; headless, writes nothing."
 "init$install"
  "Install tools brainyard relies on, by name (codex, tmux, gh, …): each only after the person says yes, with a package manager that asks nothing (brew, npm); any other install is given for the person to run. Headless, only lists the commands."
 ;; arguments, as "<tool> :arg", and result fields, as "<tool> result :field" (byj-2e8.9)
 "profile$edit :dir"
  "the project directory; this project when absent"
 "profile$edit :goal"
  "what the project is for, replacing the goal"
 "profile$edit :in"
  "in scope, one a line, replacing the list"
 "profile$edit :out"
  "out of scope, one a line, replacing the list"
 "profile$edit :done"
  "done criteria, one a line, replacing the list"
 "profile$edit :preset"
  "conservative, collaborator or autopilot"
 "profile$edit :autonomy"
  "\"axis level\" one a line (e.g. git/commit ask), set over the preset; \"axis preset\" drops one"
 "profile$edit :issues"
  "where the project's issues are kept, replacing the list: an EDN vector, one map a tracker — {:tracker :beads}, {:tracker :github :github-repo \"owner/name\"} (else the origin remote), {:tracker :linear :linear-team \"ENG\"}, {:tracker :jira :jira-site \"acme.atlassian.net\" :jira-project \"ABC\"}; :name tells two of one kind apart; [] drops them"
 "init$check :dir"
  "the project directory; this project when absent"
 "init$scaffold :dir"
  "the project directory; this project when absent"
 "init$scaffold :dry-run"
  "true: say what would be written, write nothing"
 "init$scaffold :notes"
  "the project's own section of AGENTS.md (what it is, how to build and test it, its conventions), in its own block"
 "init$beads :dir"
  "the project directory; this project when absent"
 "init$beads :prefix"
  "the issue prefix; bd's default (the directory name) when absent"
 "init$survey :dir"
  "the project directory; this project when absent"
 "init$next :dir"
  "the project directory; this project when absent"
 "init$next :examples"
  "example requests for this project, one a line, shown in place of the generic ones"
 "init$onboard :dir"
  "the project directory; this project when absent"
 "init$profile :dir"
  "the project directory; this project when absent"
 "init$profile :goal"
  "what the project is for"
 "init$profile :in"
  "in scope, one a line"
 "init$profile :out"
  "out of scope, one a line"
 "init$profile :done"
  "done criteria, one a line"
 "init$profile :preset"
  "conservative, collaborator or autopilot"
 "init$profile :autonomy"
  "axis levels apart from the preset, \"axis level\" one a line"
 "init$profile :issues"
  "the first issues, in order, one a line"
 "init$install :tools"
  "the tools to install, by name: a list, or names separated by commas or spaces"
 ;; what its tools say back to the model, as "<namespace>/<definition>" (byj-2e8.9)
 "init/tracker-problems"
  "it keeps the issues in beads, and beads is not set up here (no .beads/): /init sets it up"
 "init/tracker-problems 2"
  "it keeps the issues in GitHub, and names no :github-repo with no github.com remote here"
 "init/write-profile"
  "The person said yes when asked, shown this draft, so the profile is written as they confirmed it: .brainyard/profile.edn ("}
